---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { operator, privacyEmail } from "../../lib/site";
---

<Legal
  locale="en"
  page="support"
  title="Support"
  description="How to get help with SubEye: where to write, what to include, and answers to the things that come up most."
>
  <p>
    SubEye is built and run by one person. There is no ticket queue and no bot —
    you write to a human and a human writes back.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to write</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a> reaches {operator}
    directly. Expect a reply within a few days; anything about your personal data
    is answered within 30 days, as the <a href="/en/privacy-policy/"
      >privacy policy</a
    > says.
  </p>
  <p>
    If something is broken, three lines make it fixable in one round instead of
    four: your iPhone model and iOS version, what you tapped, and what happened
    instead of what you expected.
  </p>

  <h2>Reminders are not arriving</h2>
  <p>
    Reminders are scheduled on your device by iOS. There is no push server, so
    nothing can be re-sent from here. Check Settings → Notifications → SubEye on
    the phone first, then Settings → Notifications inside the app, which shows
    how many reminders are scheduled right now. If that number is zero while you
    have active subscriptions, that is worth an email.
  </p>

  <h2>You bought Pro and the app does not know</h2>
  <p>
    Settings → Restore purchases asks the App Store again, using whichever Apple
    Account is signed in. A new phone, a reinstall, or a different Apple Account
    are the three usual reasons. SubEye Pro is tied to the Apple Account that
    paid for it, not to your SubEye account.
  </p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Purchases go through Apple, so refunds do too — request one at <a
      href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">reportaproblem.apple.com</a
    >. SubEye cannot issue a refund itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Settings → Delete account, in the app. It removes the account and every
    subscription in it, immediately and for good. Nothing has to be requested
    from here, and it cannot be undone.
  </p>

  <h2>What SubEye cannot do</h2>
  <p>
    It does not connect to your bank, it does not read your email, it cannot see
    your real charges, and it cannot cancel a subscription on your behalf. Every
    figure in the app is arithmetic on the numbers you typed in — see the <a
      href="/en/terms-of-service/">terms of service</a
    >. There is no Android app and no web app.
  </p>
</Legal>
